  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lagos State Employment Trust Fund (LSETF)-AMTIS Skills Place Garment Construction Training</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Amtis Skills Place (Amtis) is a vocational training centre situated in Lagos, Nigeria. It was established in 2015 to bridge the increasing gap between the school curriculum and skills acquisition. Amtis has trained over 2,000 students in fashion design, automobile maintenance, makeup artistry, photography in secondary schools in Lagos and Abuja. The proposed project will train 80 youth in garment making and will place at least 50% in paid internships upon completion of the program.</narrative>
  </description>
